@@ -219,6 +220,18 @@ Browser device tokens derived from the old shared credential are revoked too.
 For SecretRef credentials, set `gateway.auth.mode` explicitly to make rotation
 eligible for hot reload. Auth-mode changes still restart the Gateway.
 
+Identity allowlist and scope changes hot-apply without restarting the Gateway.
+Already authenticated trusted-proxy users whose own admission and grants are
+unchanged stay connected, including while another user joins. Removed identities
+and identities whose grants changed reconnect under the current policy; native
+role changes retain their existing targeted reconnect behavior. In-flight
+handshakes and requests recheck committed policy, so a rejected configuration
+publication does not revoke users. Trusted-proxy plugin cookies are bound to the
+individual identity's policy. Shared credential-derived device tokens and cookies
+without a trusted-proxy identity retain their full credential-generation checks.
+Changing proxy headers, trusted proxies or auth mode retains its existing restart
+and revocation behavior.
+
 <Note>
 Changing `gateway.reload` or `gateway.remote` also does **not** trigger a restart.
 </Note>
